    "body": "Ordinary balanced rational-height shifts cannot meet the existing HHG sufficient bound. This PR adds a different selector route: translated subcritical coordinate charts, with hand-derived upper and lower bounds on universal chart coverage, plus an unexecuted, capped Sage source candidate from a fixed interval catalog through scalar replay. Useful short equations, finite-root cost and random-target yield remain unestablished. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe source retains ordinary and full modular saturation, adds explicit local subresultants as a negative control, and verifies denominator witnesses, LLL transformations, exact L1 bounds and original point relations before recovery. The local-minors shortcut remains obstructed at balanced heights for chains of length at least four. Constant/polylogarithmic chart shrink has subexponential coverage cost; this is not an extraction or complete ECDLP algorithm result. [pcc:unverified]\n\nEarlier components in this PR contribute nine generic universal-pool laws and thirteen filtration/projective-quadratic laws. Their canonical local Lean audit is271/0/0, with actual S3 semantic probes and named axiom checks. No Lean file changed in the new prototype phase; the older audit does not verify Python/Sage. Seven Python/seven JSON files parse, launcher help passes, and nine generic count/cap/fake-client development controls pass. All four final prototype PDF pages were inspected. No Sage, curve, LLL, numerical, paid or qualification run occurred. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe original paired public toy protocol is unchanged; a separate subcritical packet has fixed-control semantics. Proposed ceilings are not grants or launch requests. A source-bound runtime image, custody, actual caller/capacity and known remaining shared budget are prerequisites; the live cost/reservation record is still missing. [pcc:unverified]\n\nScoped claims PCC-20261116-8ad24e, PCC-20261116-c2eaec and PCC-20261116-2c3e0c remain unverified. All137 pinned subjects match, all106 older pins are unchanged, and the published eleven-row owner ledger is an exact byte/parsed prefix of the twelve-row chain. No independent signed verdict or native identity certificate. [pcc:unverified]\n\nReports: docs/universal-shift-pool-20261116.md; docs/balanced-height-filtration-20261116.md; docs/saturated-selector-prototype-20261116.md. The complete classical subexponential prime-field ECDLP criterion remains unmet. Hosted status must be checked on the actual published head; earlier explicit zero-step billing failures are not passes or grounds for unchanged retries/payment. [pcc:unverified]\n",
